{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "14", "M": "48", "S": "32"}}, "news": [{"title": "NBCC (India)\u2019s net profit rises 17% to \u20b9158 crore in Q1 FY27", "para": "NBCC India reported a seventeen percent growth in profit for the June 2026 quarter, achieving a net profit of \u20b9158 crore compared to \u20b9135.03 crore the previous year. However, total income experienced a minor decline of five point nine percent. As a gesture to shareholders, the board has announced an interim dividend of \u20b90.15 per equity share, equating to fifteen percent of the face value.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/nbcc-indias-net-profit-rises-17-to-158-crore-in-q1-fy27/133157957?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-339296/133157957.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Embassy Developments\u2019 net loss widens 42% to \u20b9234.40 crore in Q1 FY27", "para": "Embassy Developments has reported a consolidated net loss of \u20b9234.40 crore for the first quarter of FY27. During this time, the total consolidated income plunged to \u20b9241.28 crore. However, on a positive note, pre-sales skyrocketed by 338% on a year-on-year basis, reaching \u20b9868 crore, while collections rose by 54%, totaling around \u20b9496 crore. The board has sanctioned raising \u20b9362.62 crore through a preferential issue to enhance its financial strength.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/embassy-developments-net-loss-widens-42-to-234-40-crore-in-q1-fy27/133157804?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-115119/133157804.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Green debt share in REIT borrowings may rise to 15-17% in three years: ICRA", "para": "Outstanding green borrowing